Image Formats

A Plug-In for Mill. Put it in the "Mill Plug-Ins" folder.

  MacPaint    .mac, .pntg, or Finder type PNTG
  PICT        Version 1 and 2, .pict or .pct, or Finder type PICT
  XBM         X10 and X11 bitmaps, .xbm
  BMP         Windows 3 and OS/2 bitmaps, .bmp
  Netpbm      PBM, PGM, and PPM, plain or raw
  PNG         All color types and depths, .png or Finder type PNGf

Images show in pages and on their own, read as they arrive. Mill scales
and dithers them, and makes large ones smaller to fit its memory.

PICT version 1 is drawn by QuickDraw. Version 2 needs Color QuickDraw,
so only its images are shown, not its lines, shapes, or text. BMP: 1,
4, 8, or 24 bits, RLE4 and RLE8.

PNG: gray, palette, and truecolor, 1 to 16 bits, with or without
alpha, interlaced or not. A pixel at least half opaque is blended onto
white; one less shows the page. Mill draws a picture's pixel or the
page, nothing between, so a soft edge on a dark table cell keeps a light
fringe. Gamma is ignored: Mill dithers to black and white, so exact
tones matter less than speed. CRCs are not checked, for speed (damage
mostly shows in the compressed data anyway); to check them, turn on
Check CRCs under PNG in Mill's settings. Memory: 36K for decompressing
and two rows, about 40K for a 200 x 150 picture.
An interlaced one also keeps a quarter of its pixels until its last
pass: past 64K of them (512 x 512, or 362 x 362 with transparency) it
is too large, and shows broken.

Written from the published specifications (Apple Technical Notes 86 and
171, Inside Macintosh volumes I and V, Imaging With QuickDraw, Xlib's
XReadBitmapFile, the Windows 3.1 SDK, the OS/2 2.0 Presentation Manager
reference, Netpbm's format pages, and the PNG 1.0 specification, RFC 2083,
with RFC 1950). PNG's decompression is Mill's own.

Build: ./build.sh writes build/Image Formats.bin.
